    "### 8.4. PacBio Application: Filtering Roadmap for PacBio (SMRT/HiFi) Raw Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Dear researchers, if one day in your bioinformatics career you work with a raw dataset from the Pacific Biosciences (**PacBio**) platform, you need to fundamentally change your long-read strategy:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 1. Why Isn't Porechop Used?\n",
    "PacBio technology wraps DNA fragments with circular adapters (SMRTbell) and reads the same molecule over and over in a loop (Circular Consensus Sequencing - CCS). These circular adapters are automatically trimmed and cleaned up in the instrument's own internal software layer (at the hardware stage). Since there's no adapter left to trim in the raw data (HiFi FASTQ), **the Porechop tool is never used on PacBio data**.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 2. Change in Filtlong Parameters\n",
    "Thanks to the circular consensus reading logic, PacBio HiFi data reaches a unique level of raw read accuracy (>99.9%). Because of this high accuracy, we don't need as aggressive a quality filter with Filtlong as we do for Nanopore.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Length Threshold Raised (`--min_length 2000`):** to maximize variant-calling accuracy in PacBio data, we usually remove short artificial reads (artifacts) with a higher threshold.\n",
    "* **Quality Threshold Relaxed (`--keep_percent 95`):** since the data is already very high quality, we keep a large portion of it, around 95%, in the pool so we don't lose biological signal."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
